{
    "_readme": [
        "The colour migration's single decision. Every literal in the admin UI resolves",
        "through this file to a semantic role, and nothing else decides anything.",
        "",
        "KEYED BY PAIR, not by value. `#fff` under `background` is a surface and under",
        "`color` is a foreground; a hex-to-token map cannot tell them apart and would",
        "paint white text on white cards. The five groups come from the property:",
        "text | surface | border | shadow | icon (see lib/style-colours.mjs).",
        "",
        "HOW THE VALUES WERE CHOSEN. Not by taste: `node scripts/codemods/colour-to-token.mjs",
        "--report --context` prints every pair with the declarations it appears in, and the",
        "role is whatever those declarations are all doing. Where they were NOT all doing",
        "the same thing, the pair moved into `byFile` rather than being averaged — that is",
        "the only honest resolution, and there are eleven such cases.",
        "",
        "WHAT COLLAPSED. Three greens (#047857 #166534 #065f46) were three components'",
        "answers to 'success text'; three browns (#b45309 #92400e #78350f) to 'draft text';",
        "three reds (#b91c1c #991b1b #7f1d1d) to 'error text'. Two off-whites (#fbbf... etc.)",
        "were the same raised canvas. Those are the ~840 literals collapsing to ~40",
        "intentions the plan predicted, and each collapse is visible as one line here."
    ],

